    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two parallel equipment issues are modeled as distinct failure chains converging on the same Consequence node per instructions: (1) PS-3-2011 pressure switch fault -> CV-3-2011 opening -> Medium Runback -> FRV/steam demand mismatch -> rising S/G level -> manual trip; (2) MOV-3-1432 broken wire -> relay trip -> lost position indication -> operator manual MSIV closure. Both failure origins are traced to the single official cause node (TBD/provisional) since no cause_code/category was provided in FORM-366 FIELDS; category left 'provisional' per rule 4. AFW is explicitly stated to have automatically initiated as expected and functioned, modeled as BACKED_UP_BY. Main Feedwater remaining in service is mentioned but not modeled as a separate System since it's not tied to a failure or explicit backup role beyond restating normal operation. No previous similar occurrence LER was identified per the narrative's 'Similar Events' section, so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge emitted."
